// string.grok, which lives behind the off-by-default `grok` feature.
//
// **This directory is deliberately outside conform's reach.** `collect_probes`
// reads `tests/probes` non-recursively
// (`xtask/src/golden/mod.rs`), so nothing here is captured or run by
// `cargo xtask conform`. That is the point: the word is not in the default
// registry, and a probe for a word the default build does not bind would fail
// the default build — the wrong signal entirely.
//
// Run it by hand against both, with the feature on:
//
//     cargo build -p bund2-cli --features bund2-stdlib/grok
//     diff <(./target/oracle/release/bund script --file $PWD/tests/probes/features/library-string-grok.bund) \
//          <(./target/debug/bund2      script --file $PWD/tests/probes/features/library-string-grok.bund)
//
// Single-capture patterns only: a multi-key MAP prints in an unreproducible
// order (F76), which is why this is not simply a longer probe.

"%{WORD:w}" "hello" string.grok println
"%{NUMBER:n}" "nothing here" string.grok println
"hello" return "%{WORD:w}" string.grok. println
